# DigitalGuardian area 53: every case of fn_14_A6A8 (AcceptScriptMsg; `send` takes the
# four-character code as hex) and the scan display's fn_14_9CA4 / fn_14_9ABC (console `scan`),
# with the head (e0035000f) there and after it is deleted. Before the first Think the collision
# managers (0xE60, 0xE64) are null: the ACTV/DCTV/XAUD null arms run at f150 (layer 11's guardian
# is there, inactive, by then). Editor ids (e...): unique ids are reused across the layer load.
# XDEL with null managers: digitalguardian_msgs_del.con (a second run, it deletes the guardian).
@f30 layer 3
@f60 layer 11
# ACTV (inactive: null managers), ACTV again (active: skipped), DCTV (active: null managers),
# DCTV again (inactive: skipped), XAUD with null managers.
@f145 obj e00350060
@f150 send e00350060 0x41435456; send e00350060 0x41435456; send e00350060 0x44435456; send e00350060 0x44435456; send e00350060 0x58415544
@f160 send e00350060 0x41435456; send e0035000f Activate
# the scan with the head there (beacon down)
@f300 scan e00350060
@f360 scan e00350060
@f640 scan
# OPEN: the beacon rises (x1268 2), reaches 1.0 after 60 updates (fn_14_28D0 starts its sound)
@f800 send e00350060 0x4F50454E
@f900 scan e00350060
@f960 scan e00350060
@f1240 scan
# OPEN with x1268 1 (skipped); DCTV/ACTV with the managers built (0x128C bit 0x40 clear)
@f1400 send e00350060 0x4F50454E; send e00350060 0x44435456; send e00350060 0x41435456
# the cases with one arm each, and an unknown message (default)
@f1450 send e00350060 0x58414C44; send e00350060 0x58444D47; send e00350060 0x58524447; send e00350060 0x58484954
@f1460 send e00350060 0x494D3030; send e00350060 0x494D3031; send e00350060 0x494D3032; send e00350060 0x494D3033; send e00350060 0x494D3034
@f1470 send e00350060 0x494D3035; send e00350060 0x494D3036; send e00350060 0x494D3037; send e00350060 0x494D3038
@f1480 send e00350060 0x58435254; send e00350060 0x12345678; send e00350060 0x494D3039; send e00350060 0x47000000
# CrippledReaction sets 0x128C bit 0x40; then DCTV/ACTV wakes the second manager (0xA91C)
@f1500 fsm e00350060 CrippledReaction
@f1560 send e00350060 0x44435456; send e00350060 0x41435456
# the head is deleted: the scan without it
@f1600 send e0035000f Delete
@f1650 scan e00350060
@f1710 scan e00350060
@f1990 scan
# XAUD; then CLOS and OPEN in the same tick (OPEN sees 0x128C bit 0x08 that CLOS set). CLOS's
# delete request delivers "XDEL" (kSM_Delete, CStateManager::DispatchScriptMessages) with the
# managers built and the beacon sound playing, then removes the guardian.
@f2200 send e00350060 0x58415544
@f2210 send e00350060 0x434C4F53; send e00350060 0x4F50454E
@f2260 objs Guardian
@f2280 covdump
